# Applies to every build whose context is the repo root: web/Dockerfile (via
# docker-compose and the CI frontend job) and fly/Dockerfile (via `flyctl deploy`).
#
# Why this file has to exist. BuildKit reads .dockerignore from the *context root*, so
# web/.dockerignore stopped applying the moment web's build context moved up here — and
# fly/Dockerfile was already rooted here with no ignore file at all. With nothing to
# exclude, two things happen, both measured on this repo:
#
#   1. The context balloons.        15.85 kB / 0.3s  ->  38.74 MB / 25.8s
#   2. `COPY web/ ./web/` overlays the host's web/node_modules on top of the one
#      `npm ci` just built INSIDE the image. Node resolves the nearest node_modules
#      first, so the host copy then wins:
#          eslint resolves from web -> /app/web/node_modules/eslint   (host, mtime 08-10)
#          the npm ci copy at        -> /app/node_modules/eslint      (mtime 08-12)
#      Today the shadowed packages are dev tooling (eslint, jsdom) because workspace
#      hoisting leaves react at the root — but the mechanism shadows whatever is there,
#      and a host-built native binary would be the wrong platform for the image.
#
# Do NOT exclude backend/, web/, packages/ or fly/ — all four are copied by fly/Dockerfile.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Test/build output
web/coverage
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/.vite
mobile/.expo
mobile/android
mobile/ios

# Local runtime state — the DB is a Fly volume in production
data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Docs and design assets: nothing in any image reads these
docs
design
releases
**/*.md
!README.md
